@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+# Resume Projection Integrity Hardening Implementation Plan
+
+Contract: `specs/state.md` "Checksum-Compatible Resume Projection Integrity". Design: `docs/design/resume_projection_integrity_hardening.md`. No worktrees. Executor and loader must not grow: new logic lives in new modules under 500 lines.
+
+## Step 1 characterization (current gaps)
+- (a) `orchestrator/cli/commands/resume.py:390-406` persists observability overrides before the checksum check at `:466`; the bundle is loaded at `:424` before checksum validation.
+- (b) `orchestrator/workflow/calls.py:798` selects the callee via `workflow_import_bundle(loaded_bundle, call_alias)`; `_retry_family_base` (`:58`) uses `split('::retry::', 1)`; `_is_workflow_lisp_target` (`:41`) uses the `.orc` suffix; `frame_id_with_overrides` (`:141-152`) returns the first non-completed frame by mapping order.
+- (c) `orchestrator/loader.py:177` `yaml.load(f, Loader=PreservingLoader)` silently collapses duplicate `imports` keys.
+- (d) `orchestrator/workflow_lisp/build.py:387` sets `frontend_kind` via `replace` on the selected bundle only.
+- (e) `RunState.from_dict` indexes required keys directly and builds `ForEachState(**...)`; `_write_state`/`fail_run` round-trip through `RunState.to_dict`, dropping unknown root fields.
+- (f) `resume.py:614-621` `finally` calls `close_executor_session` then `_write_state()`.
+- (g) Frontend build artifacts go to `<workspace>/.orchestrate/build/<fingerprint>` (`build.py:376`), outside the run tree.
+- `git status --short` at start: clean.
+
+## Assumptions/Conflicts
+1. Task item 4 says "one retry lineage per boundary"; calls derive frame ids with `::visit::<n>`, so a boundary legitimately has several visit families. Interpreted per visit family; at most one running member per boundary per parent scope.
+2. Task item 6 says root projection failure changes only status/error/updated_at; a reached-call failure necessarily writes the caller/ancestor snapshots and may run finalization. Two delta classes (ROOT, REACHED-CALL) are defined in the spec.
+3. Nested frames live in the parent frame's own `call_frames`; inherited parent `::retry::` text inside a child frame id is not a child retry marker.
+4. The CLI never writes the checksum envelope (only the structural-root executor does).
+
+5. The task prose says "seven" context keys but lists eight; all eight are required.
+6. The 2026-07-13 design plan names a 2026-07-13 implementation-plan filename; this plan is dated 2026-10-18.
+
+## Steps 2-14 (each: RED tests first, then implement, run narrow selector + `pytest --collect-only`, commit; stop after 3 failed attempts and reassess)
+- 2 Typed provenance: `workflow_lisp/lowering/core.py` (`validate_lowered_workflows.validate_one`, skip `imported_workflow_bundles` identity), `build.py` (stop overwriting), `calls.py` (`_is_workflow_lisp_target`); `tests/test_workflow_lisp_frontend_kind.py`.
+- 3 YAML aliases: new `orchestrator/loader_imports_scan.py`, hook in `loader._load_workflow`; `tests/test_loader_validation.py`.
+- 4 Slots: new `workflow/resume_slots.py`, thin methods in `state_projection.py`, `CallBoundaryProjection.import_alias` set in `lowering.py`; `tests/test_workflow_state_projection.py`.
+- 5 Lineage: new `workflow/resume_retry_lineage.py`; `tests/test_resume_retry_lineage.py`.
+- 6 Auditor: new `workflow/resume_projection_integrity.py`; `tests/test_resume_projection_integrity.py`.
+- 7 State writers: `state.py`; `tests/test_state_manager.py`.
+- 8 CLI order: `cli/commands/resume.py`; `tests/test_resume_command.py`.
+- 9 Root guard: new `workflow/resume_root_guard.py`, one call site in `executor.py`; `tests/test_executor_resume_root_guard.py`.
+- 10 Reached call: `calls.py` (+ `call_resume_validation.py` if needed); `tests/test_subworkflow_calls.py`.
+- 11 Sticky failure: `executor.py`, `loops.py`, `finalization.py`; `tests/test_resume_projection_sticky_failure.py`.
+- 12 Forensic current_step: `observability/report.py`, monitor modules; `tests/test_observability_report.py`.
+- 13 Docs reconcile only. 14 Verification incl. broad `pytest -q -n 16 --dist=worksteal` in tmux and two smoke runs.
+
+## Resolutions recorded at Step 13 (docs-only reconciliation)
+- Assumption 1 (families) resolved: per-visit families, but because resume re-increments the visit counter the reached call continues the single *open* family found by lineage; several open families fail closed (see `specs/state.md`, "Frame families").
+- Assumption 2 (delta classes) resolved as written: ROOT vs REACHED-CALL.
+- Missing loop-frame rows are tolerated by the `repeat_until` terminal-form checks (restore boundaries drop them); a present row must match.
+- `StateManager.validate_checksum` falls back to the raw persisted checksum when no typed state is loaded; the CLI additionally loads typed state best-effort before the checksum check (malformed shapes are diagnosed by the audit).
+- Existing tests whose fixtures predate the contract (current_step without `step_id`, fake bundles, goldens that serialize `CallBoundaryProjection`) were updated, not deleted.
